    <bpmn:process id="W_W1962" name="W1962. Government Project Delivery &amp; Site Coordination" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Government contract delivery schedule
Frequency: Per government contract delivery milestone
Volume: ~10–15 government contracts with multiple deliveries each
Owner: VP Supply Chain
Participants: VP Supply Chain, Trade Account Manager, DC Team, Delivery Partner
Source: workflow W1962 — Government Project Delivery &amp; Site Coordination</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1962_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1962_Lane1" name="VP Supply Chain">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1962_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1962_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1962_Lane2" name="DC Team">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1962_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1962_Lane3" name="Trade Account Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1962_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1962_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1962_End10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1962_Start5" name="Government contract delivery schedule">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1962_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1962_Task6" name="Delivery planning: (a) VP Supply Chain plans delivery schedule per government…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Delivery planning: (a) VP Supply Chain plans delivery schedule per government contract, (b) coordinate with DC for pick/pack, (c) arrange delivery transport (own fleet or 3PL), (d) for project site deliveries: coordinate with government project manager for site access and unloading
Responsible (R): VP Supply Chain
Accountable (A): VP Store Operations
Duration: 2–3 days before delivery</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1962_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1962_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1962_Task7" name="Delivery execution: (a) deliver goods to government project site or designated…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Delivery execution: (a) deliver goods to government project site or designated location, (b) obtain delivery receipt signed by government receiving officer, (c) document delivery: photos of goods at site, signed DR, (d) for large deliveries: arrange unloading labor at site
Responsible (R): DC Team / Delivery Partner
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: Per delivery</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1962_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1962_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1962_Task8" name="Acceptance certificate: (a) government inspector verifies delivery against…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Acceptance certificate: (a) government inspector verifies delivery against contract specifications, (b) for construction materials: quality inspection at site, (c) obtain acceptance certificate signed by government project manager, (d) acceptance certificate required for invoice submission and payment
Responsible (R): Trade Account Manager
Accountable (A): VP Store Operations
Duration: Per delivery</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1962_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1962_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1962_Task9" name="Delivery exception handling: (a) if goods rejected: document reason, arrange…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Delivery exception handling: (a) if goods rejected: document reason, arrange replacement, negotiate timeline, (b) if partial delivery: adjust invoice accordingly, schedule remaining delivery, (c) penalty clauses: monitor on-time delivery performance to avoid government contract penalties (typically 1/10 of 1% per day of delay)
Responsible (R): Trade Account Manager / VP Supply Chain
Accountable (A): VP Store Operations
Duration: As needed</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1962_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1962_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1962_End10" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1962_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1962_Annotation11">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-380 (ensure controlled execution — Government Bid, Quotation &amp; Order Processing (PA-46.2).) | - operational: standard operating procedures; system-enforced validation rules
Owner: VP Supply Chain</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
