    <bpmn:process id="W_W1964" name="W1964. Government Bid Protest &amp; Dispute Resolution" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Bid protest filed by or against BuildRight; government contract dispute
Frequency: ~2–3 bid protests/disputes/year
Volume: Low frequency but high impact
Owner: VP Legal
Participants: VP Legal, Trade Account Manager, VP Store Operations, External Counsel
Source: workflow W1964 — Government Bid Protest &amp; Dispute Resolution</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1964_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1964_Lane1" name="VP Legal">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1964_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1964_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1964_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1964_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1964_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1964_Start3" name="Bid protest filed by or against BuildRight; government contract dispute">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1964_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1964_Task4" name="If BuildRight files protest (lost bid due to irregularity): (a) VP Legal…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: If BuildRight files protest (lost bid due to irregularity): (a) VP Legal reviews bid results for procedural irregularities per RA 9184, (b) if grounds found: file protest with BAC within prescribed period (typically 5–10 days from bid opening), (c) compile evidence: bid documents, pricing comparison, procedural violations
Responsible (R): VP Legal
Accountable (A): VP Store Operations
Duration: 3–5 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1964_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1964_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1964_Task5" name="If protest filed against BuildRight (competitor protests BuildRight&#x27;s award)…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: If protest filed against BuildRight (competitor protests BuildRight&#x27;s award): (a) VP Legal prepares defense: compile eligibility documents, technical compliance evidence, pricing justification, (b) respond to protest within prescribed period, (c) attend BAC hearing if required
Responsible (R): VP Legal
Accountable (A): VP Store Operations
Duration: 3–5 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1964_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1964_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1964_Task6" name="Contract performance dispute: (a) if government entity disputes delivery…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Contract performance dispute: (a) if government entity disputes delivery quality or timeline: document all communications, provide evidence of compliance, (b) negotiate resolution: replacement delivery, price adjustment, or mutual termination, (c) if unresolved: escalate to arbitration per contract dispute resolution clause, (d) Legal &amp; Compliance Officer maintains dispute register per VS-36
Responsible (R): VP Legal / Trade Account Manager
Accountable (A): VP Store Operations
Duration: Per dispute</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1964_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1964_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1964_End7" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1964_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1964_Annotation8">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-380 (ensure controlled execution — Government Bid, Quotation &amp; Order Processing (PA-46.2).) | - operational: VP Legal review and approval gate
Owner: VP Legal</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
